I walk down towards the beach alone.
It is already evening, but the sky is still very bright.
The sun has not started to set yet.
I look up and think back to January.
Back then I often waited for the bus after work.
It was only four o'clock in the afternoon.
But it was already pitch dark everywhere.
I stood at the bus stop and froze.
Now I have lived here for half a year.
Everything has changed.
In Mexico, the sun always went down at almost the same time.
It was like that all year.
Here I have never experienced such long days before.
The light has given the city a whole new life.
I put on my warm sweater.
Even though the sky is bright, the wind blows a bit cold from the sea.
I am looking forward to seeing the bonfire.
It will be a lovely evening with my friends.
